.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/baseline-browser-mapping Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "[`baseline-browser-mapping`](https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/packages/baseline-browser-mapping)"
.PP
By the \fRW3C WebDX Community Group\fP and contributors\&.

.PP
\fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP provides:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
An \fRArray\fP of browsers compatible with Baseline Widely available and Baseline year feature sets via the \fB`getCompatibleVersions()` function\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
An \fRArray\fP, \fRObject\fP or \fRCSV\fP as a string describing the Baseline feature set support of all browser versions included in the module's data set via the \fB`getAllVersions()` function\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
You can use \fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP to help you determine minimum browser version support for your chosen Baseline feature set; or to analyse the level of support for different Baseline feature sets in your site's traffic by joining the data with your analytics data\&.
.SH "Install for local development"
.PP
To install the package, run:

.PP
\fRnpm install --save-dev baseline-browser-mapping\fP

.PP
\fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP depends on \fRweb-features\fP and \fR@mdn/browser-compat-data\fP for core browser version selection, but the data is pre-packaged and minified\&. This package checks for updates to those modules and the supported \fBdownstream browsers\fP on a daily basis and is updated frequently\&. Consider adding a script to your \fRpackage\&.json\fP to update \fRbasesline-browser-mapping\fP and using it as part of your build process to ensure your data is as up to date as possible:

.PP
.PP
.nf
"scripts": [
  "refresh\-baseline\-browser\-mapping": "npm i \-\-save\-dev baseline\-browser\-mapping@latest"
]
.fi
.PP

.PP
If your installed version of \fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP is greater than 2 months old, you will receive a console warning advising you to update to the latest version\&.
.SH "Importing \fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP"
.PP
This module exposes two functions: \fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP and \fRgetAllVersions()\fP, both which can be imported directly from \fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import {
  getCompatibleVersions,
  getAllVersions,
} from "baseline\-browser\-mapping";
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you want to load the script and data directly in a web page without hosting it yourself, consider using a CDN:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script type="module">
  import {
    getCompatibleVersions,
    getAllVersions,
  } from "https://cdn\&.jsdelivr\&.net/npm/baseline\-browser\-mapping";
</script>
.fi
.PP
.SH "Get Baseline Widely available browser versions or Baseline year browser versions"
.PP
To get the current list of minimum browser versions compatible with Baseline Widely available features from the core browser set, call the \fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP function:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions();
.fi
.PP

.PP
Executed on 7th March 2025, the above code returns the following browser versions:

.PP
.PP
.nf
[
  { browser: "chrome", version: "105", release_date: "2022\-09\-02" },
  {
    browser: "chrome_android",
    version: "105",
    release_date: "2022\-09\-02",
  },
  { browser: "edge", version: "105", release_date: "2022\-09\-02" },
  { browser: "firefox", version: "104", release_date: "2022\-08\-23" },
  {
    browser: "firefox_android",
    version: "104",
    release_date: "2022\-08\-23",
  },
  { browser: "safari", version: "15\&.6", release_date: "2022\-09\-02" },
  {
    browser: "safari_ios",
    version: "15\&.6",
    release_date: "2022\-09\-02",
  },
];
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The minimum versions of each browser are not necessarily the final release before the Widely available cutoff date of \fRTODAY - 30 MONTHS\fP\&. Some earlier versions will have supported the full Widely available feature set\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "\fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP configuration options"
\fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP accepts an \fRObject\fP as an argument with configuration options\&. The defaults are as follows:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  targetYear: undefined,
  widelyAvailableOnDate: undefined,
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: false,
  listAllCompatibleVersions: false
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRtargetYear\fP"
The \fRtargetYear\fP option returns the minimum browser versions compatible with all \fBBaseline Newly available\fP features at the end of the specified calendar year\&. For example, calling:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions({
  targetYear: 2020,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
Returns the following versions:

.PP
.PP
.nf
[
  { browser: "chrome", version: "87", release_date: "2020\-11\-19" },
  {
    browser: "chrome_android",
    version: "87",
    release_date: "2020\-11\-19",
  },
  { browser: "edge", version: "87", release_date: "2020\-11\-19" },
  { browser: "firefox", version: "83", release_date: "2020\-11\-17" },
  {
    browser: "firefox_android",
    version: "83",
    release_date: "2020\-11\-17",
  },
  { browser: "safari", version: "14", release_date: "2020\-09\-16" },
  { browser: "safari_ios", version: "14", release_date: "2020\-09\-16" },
];
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The minimum version of each browser is not necessarily the final version released in that calendar year\&. In the above example, Firefox 84 was the final version released in 2020; however Firefox 83 supported all of the features that were interoperable at the end of 2020\&. [!WARNING] You cannot use \fRtargetYear\fP and \fRwidelyAavailableDate\fP together\&. Please only use one of these options at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "\fRwidelyAvailableOnDate\fP"
The \fRwidelyAvailableOnDate\fP option returns the minimum versions compatible with Baseline Widely available on a specified date in the format \fRYYYY-MM-DD\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions({
  widelyAvailableOnDate: `2023\-04\-05`,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
This option is useful if you provide a versioned library that targets Baseline Widely available on each version's release date and you need to provide a statement on minimum supported browser versions in your documentation\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "\fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers\fP"
Setting \fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers\fP to \fRtrue\fP will include browsers outside of the Baseline core browser set where it is possible to map those browsers to an upstream Chromium or Gecko version:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions({
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: true,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
For more information on downstream browsers, see \fBthe section on downstream browsers\fP below\&.
.SS "\fRincludeKaiOS\fP"
KaiOS is an operating system and app framework based on the Gecko engine from Firefox\&. KaiOS is based on the Gecko engine and feature support can be derived from the upstream Gecko version that each KaiOS version implements\&. However KaiOS requires other considerations beyond feature compatibility to ensure a good user experience as it runs on device types that do not have either mouse and keyboard or touch screen input in the way that all the other browsers supported by this module do\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions({
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: true,
  includeKaiOS: true,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Including KaiOS requires you to include all downstream browsers using the \fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers\fP option\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "\fRlistAllCompatibleVersions\fP"
Setting \fRlistAllCompatibleVersions\fP to true will include the minimum versions of each compatible browser, and all the subsequent versions:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getCompatibleVersions({
  listAllCompatibleVersions: true,
});
.fi
.PP
.SH "Get data for all browser versions"
.PP
You may want to obtain data on all the browser versions available in this module for use in an analytics solution or dashboard\&. To get details of each browser version's level of Baseline support, call the \fRgetAllVersions()\fP function:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { getAllVersions } from "baseline\-browser\-mapping";

getAllVersions();
.fi
.PP

.PP
By default, this function returns an \fRArray\fP of \fRObjects\fP and excludes downstream browsers:

.PP
.PP
.nf
[
  \&.\&.\&.
  {
    browser: "firefox_android", // Browser name
    version: "125", // Browser version
    release_date: "2024\-04\-16", // Release date
    year: 2023, // Baseline year feature set the version supports
    wa_compatible: true // Whether the browser version supports Widely available
  },
  \&.\&.\&.
]
.fi
.PP

.PP
For browser versions in \fR@mdn/browser-compat-data\fP that were released before Baseline can be defined, i\&.e\&. Baseline 2015, the \fRyear\fP property is always the string: \fR"pre_baseline"\fP\&.
.SS "Understanding which browsers support Newly available features"
You may want to understand which recent browser versions support all Newly available features\&. You can replace the \fRwa_compatible\fP property with a \fRsupports\fP property using the \fRuseSupport\fP option:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getAllVersions({
  useSupports: true,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
The \fRsupports\fP property is optional and has two possible values:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRwidely\fP for browser versions that support all Widely available features\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnewly\fP for browser versions that support all Newly available features\&.
.PP

.PP
Browser versions that do not support Widely or Newly available will not include the \fRsupport\fP property in the \fRarray\fP or \fRobject\fP outputs, and in the CSV output, the \fRsupport\fP column will contain an empty string\&. Browser versions that support all Newly available features also support all Widely available features\&.
.SS "\fRgetAllVersions()\fP Configuration options"
\fRgetAllVersions()\fP accepts an \fRObject\fP as an argument with configuration options\&. The defaults are as follows:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: false,
  outputFormat: "array"
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers\fP (in \fRgetAllVersions()\fP output)"
As with \fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP, you can set \fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers\fP to \fRtrue\fP to include the Chromium and Gecko downstream browsers \fBlisted below\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
getAllVersions({
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: true,
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
Downstream browsers include the same properties as core browsers, as well as the \fRengine\fPthey use and \fRengine_version\fP, for example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
[
  \&.\&.\&.
  {
    browser: "samsunginternet_android",
    version: "27\&.0",
    release_date: "2024\-11\-06",
    engine: "Blink",
    engine_version: "125",
    year: 2023,
    supports: "widely"
  },
  \&.\&.\&.
]
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRincludeKaiOS\fP (in \fRgetAllVersions()\fP output)"
As with \fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP you can include KaiOS in your output\&. The same requirement to have \fRincludeDownstreamBrowsers: true\fP applies\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
getAllVersions({
  includeDownstreamBrowsers: true,
  includeKaiOS: true,
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRoutputFormat\fP"
By default, this function returns an \fRArray\fP of \fRObjects\fP which can be manipulated in Javascript or output to JSON\&.

.PP
To return an \fRObject\fP that nests keys , set \fRoutputFormat\fP to \fRobject\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getAllVersions({
  outputFormat: "object",
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
In thise case, \fRgetAllVersions()\fP returns a nested object with the browser \fBIDs listed below\fP as keys, and versions as keys within them:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  "chrome": {
    "53": {
      "year": 2016,
      "release_date": "2016\-09\-07"
    },
    \&.\&.\&.
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Downstream browsers will include extra fields for \fRengine\fP and \fRengine_versions\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  \&.\&.\&.
  "webview_android": {
    "53": {
      "year": 2016,
      "release_date": "2016\-09\-07",
      "engine": "Blink",
      "engine_version": "53"
    },
  \&.\&.\&.
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
To return a \fRString\fP in CSV format, set \fRoutputFormat\fP to \fRcsv\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
getAllVersions({
  outputFormat: "csv",
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fRgetAllVersions\fP returns a \fRString\fP with a header row and comma-separated values for each browser version that you can write to a file or pass to another service\&. Core browsers will have "NULL" as the value for their \fRengine\fP and \fRengine_version\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
"browser","version","year","supports","release_date","engine","engine_version"
\&.\&.\&.
"chrome","24","pre_baseline","","2013\-01\-10","NULL","NULL"
\&.\&.\&.
"chrome","53","2016","","2016\-09\-07","NULL","NULL"
\&.\&.\&.
"firefox","135","2024","widely","2025\-02\-04","NULL","NULL"
"firefox","136","2024","newly","2025\-03\-04","NULL","NULL"
\&.\&.\&.
"ya_android","20\&.12","2020","year_only","2020\-12\-20","Blink","87"
\&.\&.\&.
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The above example uses \fR"includeDownstreamBrowsers": true\fP
.RE
.PP
