These files are updated on a daily basis\&.
.SH "CLI"
.PP
\fRbaseline-browser-mapping\fP includes a command line interface that exposes the same data and options as the \fRgetCompatibleVersions()\fP function\&. To learn more about using the CLI, run:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npx baseline\-browser\-mapping \-\-help
.fi
.PP
.SH "Downstream browsers"
.PP
.SS "Limitations"
The browser versions in this module come from two different sources:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
MDN's \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP module\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Parsed user agent strings provided by \fRuseragents\&.io\fP
.PP

.PP
MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP is an authoritative source of information for the browsers it contains\&. The release dates for the Baseline core browser set and the mapping of downstream browsers to Chromium versions should be considered accurate\&.

.PP
Browser mappings from useragents\&.io are provided on a best effort basis\&. They assume that browser vendors are accurately stating the Chromium version they have implemented\&. The initial set of version mappings was derived from a bulk export in November 2024\&. This version was iterated over with a Regex match looking for a major Chrome version and a corresponding version of the browser in question, e\&.g\&.:

.PP
\fRMozilla/5\&.0 (Linux; U; Android 10; en-US; STK-L21 Build/HUAWEISTK-L21) AppleWebKit/537\&.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4\&.0 Chrome/100\&.0\&.4896\&.58 UCBrowser/13\&.8\&.2\&.1324 Mobile Safari/537\&.36\fP

.PP
Shows UC Browser Mobile 13\&.8 implementing Chromium 100, and:

.PP
\fRMozilla/5\&.0 (Linux; arm_64; Android 11; Redmi Note 8 Pro) AppleWebKit/537\&.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/128\&.0\&.6613\&.123 YaBrowser/24\&.10\&.2\&.123\&.00 SA/3 Mobile Safari/537\&.36\fP

.PP
Shows Yandex Browser Mobile 24\&.10 implementing Chromium 128\&. The Chromium version from this string is mapped to the corresponding Chrome version from MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Where possible, approximate release dates have been included based on useragents\&.io "first seen" data\&. useragents\&.io does not have "first seen" dates prior to June 2020\&. However, these browsers' Baseline compatibility is determined by their Chromium or Gecko version, so their release dates are more informative than critical\&.
.RE
.PP
This data is updated on a daily basis using a \fRscript\fP triggered by a GitHub \fRaction\fP\&. Useragents\&.io provides a private API for this module which exposes the last 7 days of newly seen user agents for the currently tracked browsers\&. If a new major version of one of the tracked browsers is encountered with a Chromium version that meets or exceeds the previous latest version of that browser, it is added to the \fRsrc/data/downstream-browsers\&.json\fP file with the date it was first seen by useragents\&.io as its release date\&.

.PP
KaiOS is an exception - its upstream version mappings are handled separately from the other browsers because they happen very infrequently\&.
.SS "List of downstream browsers"
Browser  ID  Core  Source  Chrome  \fRchrome\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Chrome for Android  \fRchrome_android\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Edge  \fRedge\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Firefox  \fRfirefox\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Firefox for Android  \fRfirefox_android\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Safari  \fRsafari\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Safari on iOS  \fRsafari_ios\fP  \fRtrue\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Opera  \fRopera\fP  \fRfalse\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Opera Android  \fRopera_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  Samsung Internet  \fRsamsunginternet_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  WebView Android  \fRwebview_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  MDN \fRbrowser-compat-data\fP  QQ Browser Mobile  \fRqq_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  useragents\&.io  UC Browser Mobile  \fRuc_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  useragents\&.io  Yandex Browser Mobile  \fRya_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  useragents\&.io  KaiOS  \fRkai_os\fP  \fRfalse\fP  Manual  Facebook for Android  \fRfacebook_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  useragents\&.io  Instagram for Android  \fRinstagram_android\fP  \fRfalse\fP  useragents\&.io  

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
All the non-core browsers currently included implement Chromium or Gecko\&. Their inclusion in any of the above methods is based on the Baseline feature set supported by the Chromium or Gecko version they implement, not their release date\&. 
.RE
.PP

